<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Mozart asked for a same-day visit because he has had a runny nose, sneezing, a dry cough, a hoarse voice, and a scratchy throat for three days, since several of his pupils had colds. He has had no fever, and the throat is only mildly sore. He was frightened that the strep had come back and would hurt his kidneys again. His urine has stayed a normal color, his weight is steady, and he has no swelling of the face or legs. He has not taken ibuprofen, only acetaminophen once. He has no breathlessness, chest pain, ear pain, or rash. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Three days ago, after pupils had colds</td></tr><tr><td>Location</td><td>Nose and throat</td></tr><tr><td>Duration</td><td>Three days</td></tr><tr><td>Character</td><td>Runny nose, sneezing, dry cough, hoarseness, scratchy throat</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>Mild; still teaching</td></tr><tr><td>Timing</td><td>Worse in the mornings</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>Post-streptococcal glomerulonephritis diagnosed five weeks ago, recovering</td></tr><tr><td>Modifying factors</td><td>Better with warm drinks; one dose of acetaminophen</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>No fever, dark urine, swelling, breathlessness, or rash</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

